"""Lyra Local Satellite -- wake-word gate (wake_gate).

openWakeWord front end over the wakeword MODULE's models, all loaded
BY REFERENCE (never copied into this project):
  - feature pipeline: modules/wakeword/data/wake/melspectrogram.onnx
    + embedding_model.onnx
  - classifier: modules/wakeword/models/hey_lyra_stable_v1.onnx
    (Wakeword Stable V1, declared 2026-11-01) + its .onnx.data sidecar

This is a faithful port of the reference streaming front end
(openwakeword.utils.AudioFeatures, in the wakeword venv), which
matters: the mel model is STATEFUL across chunks (it carries 480
samples of context), so the stream must be fed in 1280-sample chunks
with the reference's exact overlap/window bookkeeping --
  - every 1280 new samples, the mel model runs over the last
    (n_new + 480) raw samples and the resulting frames are APPENDED
    to a rolling mel buffer that starts as 76 frames of ones;
  - after each chunk, new embeddings are computed for every newly
    completable 76-frame window of that buffer, in reverse order
    (the newest window first), exactly as the reference does;
  - the classifier reads the last 16 embeddings (input 'x',
    shape (1, 16, 96)); its output is already a sigmoid score.
The port was verified score-for-score against openwakeword.Model
on real clips from the module's positive pool.

HeyLyraGate.triggered(window) keeps the bridge-era call shape used
by the pipeline and the miss miner: it resets, streams the window in
1280-sample chunks, and returns (best_score >= threshold,
best_score) over every intermediate classifier read.
"""

